{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"captious-tangled-pigeon","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThree finished rollouts still keep their switches in production code. `REBAR_RECONCILER_CREATE_ROUTE` (`create_route.py:77-93`; legacy create path `apply_outbound.py:102-145`, `dispatch_one.py:363-415`, `batch_dispatch.py:251,264-269`, `apply_handlers.py:197-198`). `REBAR_RECONCILER_WRITE_FACADE` (`reconcile_helpers.py:245-256,295-296`): landed by epic RP-04 `vibrant-legal-hind` (closed) S3 as the AC6 rollback switch; its S7 `junior-lepidolite-boa` (closed) checked \"legacy facades/switches removed\", and `disturbed-antiutopic-pullet` is that epic's `session_log` and needs nothing — deleting the switch completes S7. `REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP` (readers `apply_handlers.py:282,551,589`) is set to `\"1\"` in the sole live deployment, `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml:287`. Decision: promote fail-loud to unconditional and delete all three env vars (no test hook, no injected parameter). Cites are on origin/main 083620b0 (engine paths are under `src/rebar/reconciler/` after the package move).\n\n## Approach\n1. Delete `create_route()`, `LEGACY_ROUTE`, `_LEGACY_TOKENS`, `_COORDINATOR_TOKENS`; `route_for` (`batch_dispatch.py:254-281`) returns `COORDINATOR_ROUTE` for create unconditionally; delete `_apply_outbound_create_legacy`, `_legacy_create_core`, `_legacy_record_key`, the `create_core` fallback default at `dispatch_one.py:213` (`create_core` becomes required), and the `apply_handlers.py:197-198` branch.\n2. Delete `_write_facade_enabled` and its `if not …: return` guard; `bind_operation_runtime` always composes. Delete the `applier._load_acli` ambient fallback at `applier.py:389-390,545` and the `applier._load_acli` test seam that `_resolve_pass_transport` honours: `apply()` requires `client` (raise `TypeError` when `None` and any mutation exists). `fetcher._load_acli` (`:113`) stays (fetch composes its own transport).\n3. Make the three fail-loud branches unconditional; delete the env reads and `reconcile-bridge.yml:287`; update `docs/config.md:395-403`, regenerate `docs/env-vars.md`, update `docs/user-guide.md`, add the `CHANGELOG.md` BREAKING entry.\n4. Baseline: the three `env_var` rows in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` become stale; because `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364` asserts the committed baseline equals the live tree, run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` in the same change and commit the baseline (operator-sanctioned on the epic, stated in the commit message; itemised in this ticket's comments).\n5. Tests: delete `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_apply_outbound_create_rollback.py` (`_force_legacy_route` fixture); rewrite `test_silent_noop_canary.py:160-177`, `test_fail_loud_comment_errors.py:146,180`, `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_core_seam_clean_heldout.py:226-233` to assert unconditional hard-fail; update the `test_live_mode_failure_tally.py` docstring.\n\nBREAKING: env vars `REBAR_RECONCILER_CREATE_ROUTE`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_WRITE_FACADE`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP` removed; silent sub-op no-ops and swallowed comment failures always fail the mutation.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/reconciler/{create_route,apply_outbound,dispatch_one,batch_dispatch,apply_handlers,reconcile_helpers,applier,reconcile}.py`, `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`, `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, `docs/config.md`, `docs/env-vars.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, the tests named above. Out of scope: `fetcher._load_acli`, `MODE_CAPS` and the bootstrap modes (live consumers, kept), and every other `REBAR_RECONCILER_*` variable.\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `pytest tests/unit/reconciler/mutate tests/unit/reconciler/apply -q`. Edge: `REBAR_RECONCILER_CREATE_ROUTE=legacy pytest tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_create_live_cutover_heldout.py` behaves identically (env ignored); a `comment_errors`-carrying outcome with no env set has `outcome[\"error\"]` starting `comment-errors:`; `applier.apply(mutations, pass_id, root, client=None)` with a non-empty list raises `TypeError`; `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` clean; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` prints `new=0`; `git grep -n 'REBAR_RECONCILER_\\(CREATE_ROUTE\\|WRITE_FACADE\\|FAIL_SILENT_NOOP\\)' -- src docs .github` returns only `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/release-notes.md` hits.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The three env names appear nowhere in `src/`, `.github/workflows/`, `docs/` except `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/release-notes.md` — grep.\n- [ ] `route_for(\"create\")` is `\"coordinator\"` with no env influence — unit test.\n- [ ] Silent-no-op and swallowed comment failures count toward `mutation_failures` unconditionally — canary tests.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` prints `new=0` against the committed baseline — `make lint`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"fc96-b268-b737-4b8b","parent_id":"ebf5-5d21-0124-4313","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Delete the three retired REBAR_RECONCILER_* rollback toggles and make fail-loud unconditional"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788807459767654746,"uuid":"139e3cf5-c182-4bcc-946a-60e67311d293"}